There arde two concepts:
1. Local Repository
The repository on your computer.
- main → Local main branch.
- master → Local master branch.
2. Remote Repository
The repository hosted on GitHub.
- origin → Default name of the remote repository.
- origin/main → Remote main branch.
- origin/master → Remote master branch.
Example
Git name	Meaning
main	Local main branch
master	Local master branch
origin	Remote repository
origin/main	Remote main branch
origin/master	Remote master branch


| Master |                            Main |
|---|---|
| Older default branch name        |     Newer default branch name |
| Historically used by Git        |      Adopted by GitHub as the default for new repositories in 2020 |
| Same functionality              |        Same functionality |
| No technical difference         |            No technical difference |